\section{Status}
\autoref{tab:status} lists every campaign: the values its search tuned, that search's verdict (\texttt{tune/report/}), whether \texttt{frozen.yaml} is approved, and how much of its grid is stored.
<< n_results >> of << status|length >> campaigns have grid results.

{\small
\begin{longtable}{lllrrlrr}
\caption{Per campaign: tuned values, tuning-report verdict (blocks/reviews), approval, grid runs stored/expected and diverged.}\label{tab:status}\\
\toprule
campaign & tuned & verdict & blk & rev & approved & runs & div.\\
\midrule
\endhead
<% for r in status %>
<< r.campaign|escape >> & << r.tuned|escape >> & << r.tune_verdict|escape >> & << r.blocks >> & << r.reviews >> & << 'yes' if r.approved else '\\textbf{no}' >> & << r.stored >>/<< r.expected >> & << r.diverged >>\\
<% endfor %>
\bottomrule
\end{longtable}
}

<% if sections %>
\section{Results}
Columns are the levels of \texttt{<< col|escape >>}; each campaign's rows are the combinations of <% for f in facets %>\texttt{<< f|escape >>}<% if not loop.last %>, <% endif %><% endfor %>.
Means are over seeds, the best per row in bold. $\Delta$ is a level's paired difference against the control (<< control|escape >>) by seed, marked $^*$ where $p < << alpha >>$ after the campaign's correction.
